maya: Quick follow-up from this morning's debugging: found a subtle combo of conditional-exports resolution + runtime fetch behavior causing auth headers to vanish on retries in Bun/Deno.

zara: Oof. Sounds like the earlier header-consumption bug?

maya: Related but different: when ESM import resolves to our node-edge shims via conditional exports, the edge build ends up using a small retry helper that mutates the Request object. In Deno/Bun that mutation can silently drop headers on second fetch.

sam: Can you share the minimal pattern?

maya: Sure. Pattern is: we call fetch with opts.headers being a Headers instance coming from the caller. On 401 we do: `opts.headers.set('Authorization', token)` and call fetch again. In many runtimes Headers objects are treated as frozen or are consumed. Fix is to clone headers before mutating.

maya: Example fix I landed in a branch:```js
function cloneHeaders(h){
  return new Headers(h instanceof Headers ? Array.from(h.entries()) : h || {});
}
async function retry(url, opts){
  const res = await fetch(url, opts);
  if(res.status === 401){
    const token = await refresh();
    const headers = cloneHeaders(opts.headers);
    headers.set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
    return fetch(url, { ...opts, headers });
  }
  return res;
}
```

zara: Nice. Also add a tiny export in the ESM entry so conditional exports can point to the same util instead of duplicating. That keeps parity between node/edge bundles.

sam: Agreed. Can we also add a TypeScript typing doc note? I've seen callers pass plain objects and sometimes pass frozen headers typed as Headers. The util should accept Headers | Record<string,string>.

maya: Yep; typed as `HeadersInit` in the helper. I added a short unit test for Bun + Deno that asserts server receives Authorization on retry.

infra-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/841 - add cloneHeaders util, update retries, add deno/bun integration test. CI: linux, mac, deno.

zara: Nice. One more thought: our Bun shim used `new Request(p, o)` which can drain body streams on re-use. For streaming endpoints we should avoid constructing Request unless necessary.

sam: Good call. We'll doc this in the SDK FAQ under "Edge runtime gotchas" and add a short sample for Deno import_map + bun.

maya: I'll merge the fix after CI and backport it to the last patch release.

zara: Thanks for the clear repro and fix. :thumbsup:
